            <ArticleTitle>Response to Brosch et al.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-269</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We would like to respond to Brosch et al. regarding our manuscript &quot;Expression of the Splicing Factor Gene SFRS10 Is Reduced in Human Obesity and Contributes to Enhanced Lipogenesis&quot; (Pihlajamäki et al., 2011b). Brosch performed RT-PCR in liver samples from 13 lean and 34 obese individuals, finding no differences in SFRS10 or LPIN1 expression. We wish to address points raised by Brosch, including experimental strategy and analysis of human SFRS10 expression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
